issues.suggestedFix:
Make the template match the problem statement and solution by adding a three-argument constructor to the template's StockIngredient class. For example, add:

public StockIngredient(String name, int price, int quantity) {
    this(name, price, quantity, false);
}

This preserves the existing strictValidation constructor while allowing the three-argument usage shown in the problem statement and Main. Alternatively, update the problem statement and example code to require the four-argument constructor and document the strictValidation parameter, but adding the three-arg overload is the least disruptive fix for students.
